    "content": "The SAT is a 2-hour 14-minute digital, adaptive college entrance exam, featuring two main sections: Reading and Writing, and Math, with a total score range of 400–1600. Administered by the College Board, it measures high school student readiness, with 2024–25 registration open for students to test, primarily during their junior or senior years. Key Aspects & Usage Examples Test Structure: The test consists of two sections (Reading/Writing, Math), each divided into two modules. The test is adaptive, meaning performance on the first module determines the difficulty of the second. Registration & Cost: Register via the College Board account. As of 2026, the cost is approximately $68. College Board account Test Day Requirements: You must use the Bluebook™ App on an approved laptop or tablet. Bluebook™ App Usage in Admissions: Scores are used by colleges to compare applicants alongside GPAs. Preparation: Official practice is available through the Bluebook App and Khan Academy. Bluebook App Khan Academy Synonyms and Related Terms Scholastic Assessment Test (former name) Scholastic Aptitude Test (original name) College Entrance Exam SAT Suite of Assessments (includes PSAT/NMSQT, PSAT 10, and PSAT 8/9) The average score for the class of 2023 was 1028. The test is taken on a computer or tablet, typically at a school or designated testing center.",
